---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About Daniel Reyes & The Money Margin"
  description="Meet Daniel Reyes, a 29-year-old product operations specialist in Austin, Texas, sharing first-person field guides on credit scores, debt paydown, and budgeting."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto py-8 sm:py-12">
    <!-- Breadcrumb -->
    <div class="mb-8 font-sans">
      <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold text-[#5C6B7A] mb-4">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#E67E22] transition-colors">Home</a>
        <span>/</span>
        <span class="text-[#E67E22] font-bold">About</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-[#1A2B3C] font-sans tracking-tight">
        About Daniel Reyes & The Money Margin
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs uppercase tracking-widest font-sans font-semibold text-[#5C6B7A] mt-2">
        Independent Personal Finance Field Notes • Austin, Texas
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Profile Header Card with Avatar -->
    <div class="mb-10 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl bg-white border border-[#E8E2D9] shadow-sm flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-center sm:items-start gap-6 font-sans">
      <div class="w-28 h-28 sm:w-32 sm:sm:h-32 flex-shrink-0">
        <img
          src="/images/daniel-avatar.svg"
          alt="Daniel Reyes portrait illustration"
          class="w-full h-full rounded-full shadow-sm"
          width="128"
          height="128"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="text-center sm:text-left flex-1">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-[#F3EFEA] text-xs font-bold text-[#1A2B3C] mb-2">
          <span>Author & Site Creator</span>
          <span>•</span>
          <span>Austin, TX</span>
        </div>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-[#1A2B3C] mb-1">Daniel Reyes</h2>
        <p class="text-sm font-semibold text-[#5C6B7A] mb-3">
          Product Operations Specialist • Salary ~$72,000
        </p>
        <p class="font-serif text-sm text-[#5C6B7A] leading-relaxed">
          Sharing unfiltered, real-world notes on climbing out of the minimum payment trap, navigating 24.99% card interest, and designing money systems that hold up under busy corporate schedules.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Main About Content -->
    <div class="font-serif text-[#1A2B3C] text-lg leading-[1.8] space-y-6">
      <p>
        Hi, I’m Daniel.
      </p>

      <p>
        I’m 29, and I live in Austin, Texas, with my girlfriend and our cat. By day, I work as a Product Operations Specialist at a mid-sized tech company, making about $72,000 a year.
      </p>

      <p>
        I am not a financial advisor. I don’t have a background on Wall Street, I don’t manage a seven-figure portfolio, and I don’t sell financial courses, private coaching, or credit repair subscriptions.
      </p>

      <p>
        I built <strong>The Money Margin</strong> for a much simpler, slightly embarrassing reason: between 2020 and 2022, I made almost every basic financial mistake an educated young adult with a decent salary could make.
      </p>

      <p>
        In late 2022, my credit score dropped to 612. I had three credit cards demanding payments, $18,000 left on my student loans (down from $28,000 when I graduated), and barely enough cash in checking to cover an unexpected vet visit. I wasn’t broke in the catastrophic sense, but I was living in a quiet state of constant low-grade panic—paying just enough on minimums to convince myself I was handling things, while my debt quietly grew.
      </p>

      <p>
        In March 2023, after nearly missing a payment outside a local grocery store, I stopped looking for magical shortcuts. I started logging every transaction, freezing impulsive credit usage, restructuring my debt payoffs, and testing systems that could survive normal, exhausting workweeks.
      </p>

      <p>
        It took me roughly three years of boring, repetitive habits to climb out of that loop, get my score above 730, and build a real emergency buffer.
      </p>

      <p>
        Everything on this site is an honest record of that process.
      </p>

      <p>
        I write about money from the messy middle of adult life. You will find real APR figures, side-by-side math on installment plans, exact scripts I used when calling bank representatives, and plenty of moments where I overcomplicated things or failed entirely before finding something that held up.
      </p>

      <p>
        Money advice on the internet usually comes from two extremes: people who are in full-blown crisis, or people who pretend to have everything optimized down to the cent. Most of us live in between. We earn a living, we get tired on Tuesday nights, and we just need systems that keep us honest when life gets loud.
      </p>

      <p>
        If you have a question about one of my field guides or just want to share your own experience, feel free to reach out.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Contact Callout Box -->
    <div class="mt-12 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-xl bg-[#F3EFEA] border border-[#E8E2D9] font-sans">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-start sm:items-center justify-between gap-6">
        <div>
          <span class="text-xs uppercase tracking-wider font-bold text-[#E67E22] block mb-1">Get In Touch</span>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-[#1A2B3C] mb-2">Have a question or feedback?</h3>
          <p class="font-serif text-sm text-[#5C6B7A] leading-relaxed">
            I read every message from readers navigating their own credit decisions and savings plans.
          </p>
          <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-[#1A2B3C]">
            Direct Email: <a href="mailto:wrwanshenchen@gmail.com" class="text-[#E67E22] hover:underline font-mono">wrwanshenchen@gmail.com</a>
          </p>
        </div>
        <a
          href="/contact"
          class="inline-flex items-center px-5 py-3 rounded-md bg-[#1A2B3C] text-white font-bold text-sm hover:bg-[#E67E22] transition-colors whitespace-nowrap shadow-sm"
        >
          Go to Contact Page &rarr;
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
